  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "The checkout-web release 5c6d7e8 was meant to receive 1% of traffic as a canary, but the traffic router parsed the canary weight as 100 instead of 1 and routed 100% of checkout-web traffic to the new build. That build has a bug (a TypeError on a null cart total in the render path), so once it was serving everyone the 500 rate jumped to ~71%. The bug would have been caught at 1%; the routing misconfiguration is what made it a full outage.",
    "evidence_path": [
      "deploy-system INFO at 11:18: checkout-web 5c6d7e8 released as canary weight=1%",
      "traffic-router WARN: canary weight parsed as 100 (expected 1); all checkout-web traffic routed to 5c6d7e8",
      "canary_traffic_share jumps from 0 to 1.0",
      "checkout-web ERROR: unhandled TypeError in the 5c6d7e8 render path; 5xx rate ~71%",
      "errors clear once traffic is shifted back to the previous build"
    ],
    "fix": "Halt the canary and shift traffic back (done). Fix the canary-weight parsing in the traffic router and add a guard that rejects a canary weight above a sane ceiling. Separately, fix and re-test the null-cart-total bug before re-releasing.",
    "should_escalate": false
  }
}
